"""Cascade room copy, verbatim from plan/room-texts.md (2026-11-12)."""

CASCADE_ROOM_GRANT_NUDGE = "(For you alone, never say this out loud: the participant is waiting for you to answer their last line, the one just above. Answer that line, not an earlier one and not a colleague's. Reply now, in character, one or two sentences.)"

CASCADE_ROOM_UNHEARD_NUDGE = '(For you alone, never say this out loud: the participant just said something to you, but you did not catch any of it. Do not guess it and do not answer anything said earlier. In character, ask them in one short sentence to say it again, as anyone in the room would, without mentioning the line or the sound.)'

ROOM_RULE_CASCADE = "\n\nThe other people in this room are your colleagues. You will receive notes in parentheses telling you what a colleague just said. They are context only. Never read them out and never narrate what a colleague said (no 'Casey just said...'): respond as someone who heard it, in your own words. Never ask a colleague to clarify what they mean, and never answer a colleague's line as if the participant had said it.\n\nWhat the participant says reaches you as plain lines, without parentheses. Answer the last thing the participant actually said to you, or stay quiet. Never say that you did not understand or did not catch something unless a note tells you that you did not catch the participant's last line; then ask them, in one short sentence, to say it again. If the participant addresses someone else by name, stay silent and let them answer. Do not repeat or rephrase what another person just said, and do not answer every turn: leave room for quieter colleagues."
